        "id": 187642,
        "name": "grysqrl",
        "username": "grysqrl",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/grysqrl/{size}/1909_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-01-01T18:04:56.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Won this one on the first try. Had some pretty good cards to start with:</p><ul>\n<li>Stun Bolt neutralized a lot of Friction's damage</li>\n<li>Ball Lightning took out both of Blade's Ongoings and made quick work of Impulsion Beam (which is a pretty harmless device to get first round, when multiple powers and plays are not too common)</li>\n<li>Driving Mantis redirected a ton of little shots back at the villains. This was particularly nice when Blade played Regression Darts. I had Driving Mantis in play the whole game.</li>\n</ul><p><span>The environment was pretty benign. Never got an Entry Point. Frost's Cryo Chamber was actually pretty nice for tearing through villain targets (again, Driving Mantis was helpful).</span></p><p><span>I took out Friction first, then Blade, then Proletariat.&nbsp;</span>Proletariat was barely involved in the fight. An early Regroup and Recover wiped out his clones and then Tempest kept putting Flanking Maneuvers back on top of his deck.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:13:28.112Z",
